and arrow that causes people to develop Stands? Because that sounds more Mage than Werewolf. Stands are Avatars when you get right down to it.<br /> <br /> I'm thinking a Talisman that, when it strikes someone, it can force an Awakening. The downside to the item is that it's not a sure thing (because no method for engineering an Awakening ever is). If the target fails to Awaken, the arrow straight up kills them. So it's a lot faster and easier than making the person read (and understand) a Primer, but with a critically severe cost for failure. It's a gamble, really, and a steep one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T00:07:58-07:00","id":975403,"title":"","content":"I love to create crazy mash-up mixing a lot of things from main geek IPs (Star Wars, Star Treck, Farscape, Andromeda, Dune, Warhammer 40.000, Mass Effect, Dead Space, Resident Evil, etc). It is a surprise for players to find supernatural enemies in a high-tech sci-fi campaing. One of my last ideas is mixing the background of the RPGs Starfinder(comingsoon), Eclise Phase and Kult: lost divinity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Tell me what you brag and I will tell you what you lack&quot; (Spanish saying)<br /> <br /> \u00abThe Master Confucius said: \u201cThe noble man is in harmony but does not follow the crowd. The inferior man follows the crowd, but is not in harmony\u201d\u00bb (Anaclet 13:23)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11152-luis-carlos","name":"Luis Carlos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"258"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T04:41:07-07:00","id":975469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/975058-videogames-anime-movie-influences-in-your-games?p=975384#post975384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The bow and arrow that causes people to develop Stands? Because that sounds more Mage than Werewolf. Stands are Avatars when you get right down to it.<br /> <br /> I'm thinking a Talisman that, when it strikes someone, it can force an Awakening. The downside to the item is that it's not a sure thing (because no method for engineering an Awakening ever is). If the target fails to Awaken, the arrow straight up kills them. So it's a lot faster and easier than making the person read (and understand) a Primer, but with a critically severe cost for failure. It's a gamble, really, and a steep one.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wanted it to have a similar effect but for another purpouse, to fit within the Werewolf Lore<br /> <br /> That, And i been thinking on how to create a villian with Dio's Powers for werewolf","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T13:10:11-07:00","id":975671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/975058-videogames-anime-movie-influences-in-your-games#post975058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">so, whenever i have a new player and i have to explain Pentex to them. i just say &quot;Umbrella corp from Resident Evil, but more subtil.&quot;, and thanks to that im turning NEMESIS into a Fomori... so my question is, have you been directly or indirectly influenced by videogames or movies or anime or comics for a game/character/plot?</div> </div> </div> </div>Influence.. Quite a few actually. I made a SW game based on the Bruce willis film Tears of the sun. <br /> I made a monster for ADND based on that wingged lizard thinggy in pitch black. <br /> But i think i mostly delve into film/comic references more to get a idea/image of something over quicker..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T03:27:19-07:00","id":975903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/975058-videogames-anime-movie-influences-in-your-games#post975058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">so, whenever i have a new player and i have to explain Pentex to them. i just say &quot;Umbrella corp from Resident Evil, but more subtil.&quot;, and thanks to that im turning NEMESIS into a Fomori...</div> </div> </div> </div>I was afraid of Nemesis as a kid (to the point of being afraid of the dark sometimes), after watching some dudes play <i>Resident Evil</i>, and THEN a year or so later browsing a PC magazine and stumbling onto a spread of his face. :&lt;<br /> Defiler Wyrm worship seems like an ideal fit for <i>Resident Evil</i>'s events.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 09-25-2016, 06:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T06:05:38-07:00","id":975920,"title":"","content":"If you're looking for Fomori material, &quot;Parasyte: The Maxim&quot; is a fairly recent anime (based on a manga) that might be up your alley. You could almost reframe the story as a high-autonomy fomor in a city where something like a Magadon factory explosion released a ton of bane-tainted toxins into the population. (NSFW: Gore)<br /> <br /> If you're just looking for power-suite inspiration, I would also recommend &quot;Basilisk: Kouga Ninpou Chou&quot; for ideas of unique fomori. (Keeping in mind that your average fomori only has a few abilities and probably goes splat in a hit or two from a Garou... but these would work well for the higher-powered &quot;Elite&quot; types)(NSFW: Gore, some nudity IIRC)<br /> <br /> For setting, I enjoy getting in the mood with movies like the Blade Trilogy, Hackers, Highlander (Particularly the TV series), The X-Files, Dark City, Johnny Mnemonic, Akira, Spriggan, etc. oWoD is still ultimately a product of the 90s angst era and most of the good material still comes from around there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my mediocre WoD/Aeon/Exalted art at <a href=\"http://blackspinel.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://blackspinel.deviantart.com</a> ! It'll make you go &quot;Yup! That's pretty mediocre!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12162-crusher-of-cities","name":"Crusher-of-Cities","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12162_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T09:56:30-07:00","id":975986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crusher-of-Cities</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/975058-videogames-anime-movie-influences-in-your-games?p=975920#post975920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you're looking for Fomori material, &quot;Parasyte: The Maxim&quot; is a fairly recent anime (based on a manga) that might be up your alley. You could almost reframe the story as a high-autonomy fomor in a city where something like a Magadon factory explosion released a ton of bane-tainted toxins into the population. (NSFW: Gore)<br /> <br /> If you're just looking for power-suite inspiration, I would also recommend &quot;Basilisk: Kouga Ninpou Chou&quot; for ideas of unique fomori. (Keeping in mind that your average fomori only has a few abilities and probably goes splat in a hit or two from a Garou... but these would work well for the higher-powered &quot;Elite&quot; types)(NSFW: Gore, some nudity IIRC)<br /> <br /> For setting, I enjoy getting in the mood with movies like the Blade Trilogy, Hackers, Highlander (Particularly the TV series), The X-Files, Dark City, Johnny Mnemonic, Akira, Spriggan, etc. oWoD is still ultimately a product of the 90s angst era and most of the good material still comes from around there.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Where can each of those anime be found?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T10:54:46-07:00","id":976016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fat Larry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/975058-videogames-anime-movie-influences-in-your-games?p=975986#post975986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where can each of those anime be found?</div> </div> </div> </div>Um...I'm pretty sure the answer violates the forum rules, so...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T12:11:50-07:00","id":976039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/975058-videogames-anime-movie-influences-in-your-games?p=976016#post976016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b