nts":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T15:12:19-07:00","id":976747,"title":"","content":"I actually try to use reality as much as possible (spiced up with extra darkness and an exaggerated missery). Imagine reality plus vampires and banes and actual demons and mages trying to lock everyone down. That said world of darkness by default uses movies for inspiration, be it the matrix for the jackets, glasses and rooftop leaping or Terminator and hit-marks. I use everything they use. But i try to keep everything so it logistically works. I'm not going to make something so terrible that it'd cause a system to shut down. I think the books have great stuff and some great artwork and I think they're often inspiration enough (even though the quality can drop terribly) <br /> <br /> I use Batman's Gotham for inspiration. I'd never call the city Gotham, but it's got a great standard for world of darkness cities- More concrete and less glass and steel, more alleyways, Imposingly tall structures, more crime and corruption. More poverty. I don't use a colourful cast of publicly known villains,but I do use <br /> Why would you want to live in such a city? Well, it's better than most of the other cities. <br /> The town from the lost boys is a pretty good example for an american tourist town. I also think the setting of &quot;The warriors&quot; portrays a good city. John Niven's books are good for your entry level high fliers if you don't wanna go ultra-decadent but still go kinda bad. <br /> <br /> For schools, I use korean manwhua, which often make their schools look like a bullying paradise. Complete with vandalism, sexual abuse, and a mentality that says the senior can do what they want to the junior. The suicide rates of korean students is now the suicide rates for... less suicide prone countries. Korea itself considers education an abattoir.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Signatures are for terrible people who want to be caught.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12414-flower-innocent","name":"Flower,Innocent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T01:20:34-07:00","id":977657,"title":"","content":"Oh yes, heavily influenced by movies such as Dark City, Reservoir Dogs, the Departed, Lost Highway,Phantoms, Event Horizon and so forth for many of my campaigns. Games not as much since the character is more tied to their specific world/setting in most cases. However there was probably some small bit of influence from Eternal Darkness I'm guessing. Shows are a big influence sometimes, for instance the dark themes and overtones of Angel, BSG, Twin Peaks, X-Files, Lazarus Man, Twilight Zone. Also certain genres of anything, like neo-noir, space horror, and so forth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2456-zeroninja","name":"zeroninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}